IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-core`
IMPORT `cla-liability`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in cla-liability.l4 (Part 1A ss 5H, 5I,
-- 5L; Part 3; Part 6; Part 7 Division 1). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was
-- copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases -- defences and limits on liability`

`general` MEANS `negligence, or another claim for death or personal injury not listed here`
`intent` MEANS `an intentional act the defendant did meaning to injure or kill`
`sexual` MEANS `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct by the defendant`
`vicarious` MEANS `vicarious liability for someone else's intentional act or sexual misconduct`
`dust` MEANS `a dust disease claim of the kind brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal`
`MAIA` MEANS `a motor accident claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017`
`statutory` MEANS `statutory compensation or a statutory benefit`

`so` MEANS `the court has found that it is so`
`not so` MEANS `the court has found that it is not so`
`undecided` MEANS `the court has not decided`

`sport` MEANS `a sport, organised or not`
`leisure` MEANS `something done for enjoyment, relaxation or leisure`
`beach` MEANS `something done at a place where people ordinarily play sport or relax, such as a beach or park`
`no activity` MEANS `none of these activities`

`parent` MEANS `the victim's parent, or a person with parental responsibility for the victim`
`spouse` MEANS `the victim's spouse or partner (the last one, if more than one would qualify)`
`child of victim` MEANS `the victim's child or stepchild, or a person the victim has parental responsibility for`
`sibling` MEANS `the victim's brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister, stepbrother or stepsister`
`not close` MEANS `another relative, a friend, or no relation`

`n/a` MEANS `this section does not apply to my claim`
`open amount` MEANS `the Act does not settle the amount`

`s 50 n/a` MEANS `section 50 does not apply to my claim`
`no damages s 50` MEANS `no damages: the court is not satisfied the injury would likely have happened even if I had not been intoxicated`
`reduced` MEANS `my damages are reduced by at least 25% for presumed contributory negligence`
`no reduction` MEANS `section 50 does not reduce my damages: the court is satisfied my intoxication did not contribute`
`s 50 open` MEANS `the Act does not settle what section 50 does yet`

`defend` MEANS `to defend themselves or another person`
`liberty` MEANS `to prevent or end the unlawful deprivation of their own or another person's liberty`
`property` MEANS `to protect property from unlawful taking, destruction, damage or interference`
`trespass` MEANS `to prevent criminal trespass on land or premises, or remove a trespasser`
`no purpose` MEANS `none of these purposes`

`self-defence` MEANS `the defendant is not liable to me: self-defence under section 52`
`s 53` MEANS `no damages unless the court finds the case exceptional and refusing damages harsh and unjust, and then none for non-economic loss (section 53)`
`no protection` MEANS `sections 52 and 53 do not protect the defendant on these facts`
`self-defence open` MEANS `the Act does not settle the self-defence question yet`

`offence` MEANS `an offence`
`impaired` MEANS `not an offence only because of my mental health impairment or cognitive impairment at the time`
`no offence` MEANS `not an offence`
`undecided conduct` MEANS `the court has not decided what my conduct was`

`s 54 bars` MEANS `no damages: section 54 bars my claim`
`s 54A limits` MEANS `no damages for non-economic loss or for lost earnings (section 54A)`
`no limit` MEANS `sections 54 and 54A do not limit my damages`
`offence open` MEANS `the Act does not settle the offence question`

§§ `s 5H -- no duty to warn of an obvious risk`

-- Arguments: kind of claim, obvious, I asked, a written law required a warning, professional service risk.
#ASSERT `Does section 5H remove the duty to warn me` `general` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 5H remove the duty to warn me` `general` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5H remove the duty to warn me` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5H remove the duty to warn me` `general` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5H remove the duty to warn me` `general` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5H remove the duty to warn me` `MAIA` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 5H remove the duty to warn me` `statutory` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5H remove the duty to warn me` `vicarious` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 5I -- inherent risk`

#ASSERT `Does section 5I stop my claim` `general` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 5I stop my claim` `general` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5I stop my claim` `general` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5I stop my claim` `sexual` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 5J-5L -- dangerous recreational activities`

-- Arguments: kind of claim, taking part myself, the activity, significant risk of physical harm, harm from an obvious
-- risk.
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `general` TRUE `sport` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `general` TRUE `leisure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `general` TRUE `beach` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `general` TRUE `no activity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `general` FALSE `sport` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `general` TRUE `sport` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `general` TRUE `sport` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A failed condition beats the open one.
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `general` TRUE `no activity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3B(2): Division 5 does not apply to motor accidents.
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `MAIA` TRUE `sport` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 5L stop my claim` `vicarious` TRUE `sport` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 3 -- mental harm`

-- ss 30, 31. Arguments: kind of claim, from negligence, pure mental harm, shock at another being killed, injured or put
-- in peril, witnessed at the scene, who I am to the victim, the victim could not recover, recognised psychiatric
-- illness. JUST TRUE = barred.
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `not close` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `parent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `spouse` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `child of victim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sibling` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `not close` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 30(4): the victim could not recover.
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `parent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 31: not a recognised psychiatric illness, with or without shock at another's peril.
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `parent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `not close` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `not close` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Consequential mental harm, and a claim not in negligence: these sections do not bite.
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `not close` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `general` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `not close` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3B(2): Part 3 applies to motor accidents; not to an act meant to injure.
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `MAIA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `not close` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do sections 30 and 31 stop my claim for pure mental harm` `intent` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `not close` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 30(3). Arguments: kind of claim, damages before reduction, the victim's reduction (%).
#ASSERT `My damages for pure mental harm after the victim's reduction` `general` 100000 30 EQUALS `the amount is` 70000
#ASSERT `My damages for pure mental harm after the victim's reduction` `general` 100000 0 EQUALS `the amount is` 100000
#ASSERT `My damages for pure mental harm after the victim's reduction` `general` 100000 100 EQUALS `the amount is` 0
#ASSERT `My damages for pure mental harm after the victim's reduction` `sexual` 100000 30 EQUALS `n/a`
#ASSERT `My damages for pure mental harm after the victim's reduction` `vicarious` 100000 30 EQUALS `open amount`

-- s 33. Arguments: kind of claim, from negligence, followed my own injury, recognised psychiatric illness.
#ASSERT `Does section 33 stop my economic loss claim for consequential mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 33 stop my economic loss claim for consequential mental harm` `general` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 33 stop my economic loss claim for consequential mental harm` `general` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 33 stop my economic loss claim for consequential mental harm` `general` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 33 stop my economic loss claim for consequential mental harm` `dust` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 6 -- intoxication`

-- s 50. Arguments: kind of claim, intoxicated and impaired, finding not self-induced, finding likely to have happened
-- anyway, finding intoxication did not contribute.
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `general` TRUE `not so` `so` `not so` EQUALS `reduced`
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `general` TRUE `not so` `so` `so` EQUALS `no reduction`
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `general` TRUE `not so` `not so` `undecided` EQUALS `no damages s 50`
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `general` TRUE `so` `not so` `not so` EQUALS `s 50 n/a`
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `general` FALSE `not so` `not so` `not so` EQUALS `s 50 n/a`
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `general` TRUE `undecided` `so` `not so` EQUALS `s 50 open`
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `general` TRUE `not so` `undecided` `not so` EQUALS `s 50 open`
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `general` TRUE `not so` `so` `undecided` EQUALS `s 50 open`
-- s 3B(2) keeps only s 49 of Part 6 for motor accidents.
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `MAIA` TRUE `not so` `so` `not so` EQUALS `s 50 n/a`
#ASSERT `What does section 50 do to my claim` `vicarious` TRUE `not so` `so` `not so` EQUALS `s 50 open`

§§ `Part 7 -- self-defence`

-- ss 52, 53. Arguments: kind of claim, the defendant's purpose, my conduct unlawful, the court's finding that it was a
-- reasonable response, death intentionally or recklessly inflicted.
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `defend` TRUE `so` FALSE EQUALS `self-defence`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `liberty` TRUE `so` FALSE EQUALS `self-defence`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `defend` TRUE `not so` FALSE EQUALS `s 53`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `defend` TRUE `undecided` FALSE EQUALS `self-defence open`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `no purpose` TRUE `so` FALSE EQUALS `no protection`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `defend` FALSE `so` FALSE EQUALS `no protection`
-- s 52(3): death inflicted only to protect property or deal with a trespasser.
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `property` TRUE `so` TRUE EQUALS `no protection`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `trespass` TRUE `so` TRUE EQUALS `no protection`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `defend` TRUE `so` TRUE EQUALS `self-defence`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `general` `property` TRUE `so` FALSE EQUALS `self-defence`
-- s 3B(1)(a): Part 7 is kept for an act meant to injure, not for sexual misconduct.
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `sexual` `defend` TRUE `so` FALSE EQUALS `no protection`
#ASSERT `Can the defendant rely on self-defence` `intent` `defend` TRUE `so` FALSE EQUALS `self-defence`

§§ `Part 7 -- my own offence`

-- ss 54, 54A. Arguments: kind of claim, hurt during or after my conduct, my conduct, maximum imprisonment (months),
-- the court's finding that it contributed materially, the defendant's conduct an offence, would have been but for the
-- defendant's impairment.
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `offence` 6 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 54 bars`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `offence` 5 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `offence` 6 `not so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` FALSE `offence` 6 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `offence` 6 `so` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
-- s 54(2) speaks only of the defendant's conduct that "constitutes an offence".
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `offence` 6 `so` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 54 bars`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `impaired` 6 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 54A limits`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `impaired` 6 `so` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `impaired` 6 `so` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `impaired` 5 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `no offence` 24 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `MAIA` TRUE `offence` 12 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 54 bars`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `sexual` TRUE `offence` 12 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `vicarious` TRUE `offence` 12 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `offence open`
-- The court's findings under s 54(1) and s 54A(1): undecided leaves the answer open only where it matters.
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `offence` 6 `undecided` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `offence open`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `undecided conduct` 6 `so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `offence open`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `impaired` 6 `undecided` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `offence open`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `undecided conduct` 6 `not so` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `undecided conduct` 6 `undecided` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `no offence` 6 `undecided` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `What does my own offence mean for my claim` `general` TRUE `undecided conduct` 5 `undecided` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
